name: files
boss: CopyPasta
flavor: Every copy is a ghost of the original.
brief: Six commands move bytes around: cp copies, mv renames or moves, rm
brief: deletes, mkdir and rmdir make and unmake directories, touch creates an
brief: empty file or bumps its timestamp.
brief:
brief: Two of them are quietly dangerous. cp and mv overwrite the destination
brief: without asking. -n refuses to, -i asks first. Learn those two flags now
brief: and you will not need to learn them from a loss later.
---
q: copy @cfg@ to @cfg2@
a: cp @cfg@ @cfg2@
state: exists:@cfg2@
ref: cp
teach: cp
---
q: copy @txt@ into the @dir@ directory, keeping its name
a: cp @txt@ @dir@/
a: cp @txt@ @dir@
state: exists:@dir@/@txt@
ref: cp
teach: cp
---
q: copy the whole @dir@ directory, and everything inside it, to @dir2@-copy
a: cp -r @dir@ @dir2@-copy
a: cp -R @dir@ @dir2@-copy
a: cp -a @dir@ @dir2@-copy
state: exists:@dir2@-copy
ref: cp
teach: cp -r
hint: the flag cp calls "Recurse"
---
q: copy @cfg@ to @cfg2@, but refuse to overwrite it if it already exists
a: cp -n @cfg@ @cfg2@
ref: cp
teach: cp -n
hint: n for "no clobber"
---
q: copy @txt@ to @txt@.bak preserving its timestamps and permissions
a: cp -p @txt@ @txt@.bak
a: cp -a @txt@ @txt@.bak
state: exists:@txt@.bak
ref: cp
teach: cp -p
hint: p for preserve
---
q: copy @dir@ to @dir2@-archive preserving everything -- one flag, not three
a: cp -a @dir@ @dir2@-archive
state: exists:@dir2@-archive
ref: cp
teach: cp -a
hint: cp calls it "Same as -dpR"
---
q: rename @txt@ to @word@.txt
a: mv @txt@ @word@.txt
state: exists:@word@.txt
ref: mv
teach: mv
---
q: move @cfg@ into @dir@/
a: mv @cfg@ @dir@/
a: mv @cfg@ @dir@
state: exists:@dir@/@cfg@
ref: mv
teach: mv
---
q: move @txt@ to @dir@/, but never overwrite a file already there
a: mv -n @txt@ @dir@/
a: mv -n @txt@ @dir@
ref: mv
teach: mv -n
---
q: delete @txt@
a: rm @txt@
state: gone:@txt@
ref: rm
teach: rm
---
q: delete @dir@ and everything inside it
a: rm -r @dir@
a: rm -rf @dir@
state: gone:@dir@
ref: rm
teach: rm -r
---
q: delete @txt@ without complaining if it is already gone
a: rm -f @txt@
ref: rm
teach: rm -f
hint: f for force -- it also silences the "no such file" error
---
q: %make% a directory called @word@
a: mkdir @word@
state: exists:@word@
ref: mkdir
teach: mkdir
---
q: %make% @dir@/@word@/deep, making the missing parent directories too
a: mkdir -p @dir@/@word@/deep
state: exists:@dir@/@word@/deep
ref: mkdir
teach: mkdir -p
hint: p for parents
---
q: %make% a directory @word@ that only you can enter, using a numeric mode
a: mkdir -m 700 @word@
state: exists:@word@
ref: mkdir
teach: mkdir -m
---
q: remove the empty directory @word@ -- create it first if you like
a: rmdir @word@
ref: rmdir
teach: rmdir
---
q: %make% an empty file called @word@.txt
a: touch @word@.txt
a: > @word@.txt
state: exists:@word@.txt
ref: touch
teach: touch
---
q: update the timestamp on @txt@ to now, without changing its contents
a: touch @txt@
state: match:@txt@:rotate
ref: touch
teach: touch
---
q: update @txt@'s timestamp but do NOT create it if it is missing
a: touch -c @txt@
ref: touch
teach: touch -c
---
q: %make% a symbolic link called @word@-link pointing at @txt@
a: ln -s @txt@ @word@-link
state: exists:@word@-link
ref: ln
teach: ln -s
hint: s for symbolic; without it you get a hard link
---
q: %make% a hard link called @word@-hard to @txt@
a: ln @txt@ @word@-hard
state: exists:@word@-hard
ref: ln
teach: ln
---
q: %make% a symlink @word@-link to @txt@, replacing it if it already exists
a: ln -sf @txt@ @word@-link
a: ln -fs @txt@ @word@-link
state: exists:@word@-link
ref: ln
teach: ln -f
---
q: copy @cfg@ to @cfg2@, asking before it would overwrite anything
a: cp -i @cfg@ @cfg2@
ref: cp
teach: cp -i
---
q: copy @cfg@ over @cfg2@ forcing it through even if the target resists
a: cp -f @cfg@ @cfg2@
state: exists:@cfg2@
ref: cp
teach: cp -f
---
q: move @txt@ to @word@.txt, asking first if that would overwrite something
a: mv -i @txt@ @word@.txt
ref: mv
teach: mv -i
---
q: move @txt@ to @word@.txt, forcing it without any prompt
a: mv -f @txt@ @word@.txt
state: exists:@word@.txt
ref: mv
teach: mv -f
---
q: delete @txt@ but ask for confirmation first
a: rm -i @txt@
ref: rm
teach: rm -i
---
q: remove @dir@/@word@/deep and any parent directories left empty behind it
a: mkdir -p @dir@/@word@/deep && rmdir -p @dir@/@word@/deep
ref: rmdir
teach: rmdir -p
---
q: %make% a named pipe called @word@.fifo
a: mkfifo @word@.fifo
state: exists:@word@.fifo
ref: mkfifo
teach: mkfifo
---
q: %make% a named pipe readable and writable only by you
a: mkfifo -m 600 @word@.fifo
state: exists:@word@.fifo
ref: mkfifo
teach: mkfifo -m
---
q: %make% a temporary file with a name nothing else will collide with
a: mktemp
out: ^/
ref: mktemp
teach: mktemp
---
q: %make% a temporary directory rather than a file
a: mktemp -d
out: ^/
ref: mktemp
teach: mktemp -d
---
q: %make% a temporary name without actually creating anything
a: mktemp -u
out: ^/
ref: mktemp
teach: mktemp -u
---
q: %make% a temporary file, staying silent if it cannot
a: mktemp -q
out: ^/
ref: mktemp
teach: mktemp -q
